{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>הנה בטני</b> — by way of parable, like the expression <b>בטנך תאכל ומעיך תמלא</b>, like <b>כאובות חדשים</b>. Some say it is as the words of the rabbis: a person should not put his head under an <i>ov</i>. And most of the commentators said: they are wineskins, and this is correct, for <b>אל תפנו אל האובות</b> — the essence of their faith is like wineskins."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes three biblical phrases: הבטנך תאכל ומעיך תמלא (Proverbs 20:30), כאובות חדשים (Job 32:19, the lemma under discussion), and אל תפנו אל האובות (Leviticus 19:31 / 20:6/27). The word אוב can mean 'wineskin' or refer to necromancy; he plays on both senses. The final clause is hyper-literal as the Hebrew is compressed and elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:18.466600446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}